#
# Let this notice through, in Sutra. A Watchfire emergency always goes
# through. Otherwise a notice goes through when it is not quiet, when its
# sender is on the allow list, or when the same caller called before within
# 3 minutes: gap is the seconds since that earlier call, -1 when there was
# none. quiet, allowed and emergency are one-digit flags (above 0: yes); a
# negative flag, or a gap past s9(9), does not fit: refused.
record let-through
  quiet: 9
  allowed: 9
  gap: s9(9)
  emergency: 9
procedure
  if emergency > 0
    answer 0 = 0
  end-if
  answer quiet < 1 or allowed > 0 or gap >= 0 and gap <= 180
